  "rationale": "Each test targets a logical property that any correct solution must satisfy, as derived from the specification. The focus is on invariants (output shape, value range), certificates (verifying claimed steps produce an m-perfect pair), and metamorphic relations (symmetry in x and y). The code's suspicious branch when x ≤ 0 and y > 0 is targeted by test_negative_positive_case_verification, which verifies the reported steps actually lead to m-perfection. The weakest test is test_output_is_integer_or_minus_one, which only checks output format; it would be dropped first if space were needed.",
