    # Since 1..K are not necessarily all lunlun, but the first K lunlun numbers include 1..K only for K<=9.
    # For K>9, the K-th lunlun number must be >= K because among 1..K, not all are lunlun, but the sequence grows slower.
    # Actually, a trivial lower bound: ans >= 1 always holds.
    assert ans >= 1"
    },
    {
