        k1 = int(run(x).strip())
        # Build new input with n' = n + x, same x, y.
        new_input = f"1\n{xx} {yy} {nn + xx}"
        k2 = int(run(new_input).strip())
        # Because n increased by x, the next candidate with same remainder is k1 + x,
        # so k2 must be either k1 or k1 + x (if k1 + x ≤ n + x).
        # Actually k2 must be the maximum for n', so k2 >= k1 and k2 ≡ y (mod x).
